      "title": "Match",
      "lastEdited": "2026-03-14T09:15:00.000Z",
      "content": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "text": "Matching means putting both hands on the same hold to stabilize before the next move." },
        { "type": "list", "style": "bulleted", "items": ["Helps with controlled movement", "Often taught to beginners", "Useful in tight sequences"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "crimp",
      "title": "Crimp",
      "lastEdited": "2026-03-14T09:20:00.000Z",
      "content": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "text": "A crimp is a small edge hold gripped with bent fingers and high finger tension." },
        { "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "Training note" },
        { "type": "paragraph", "text": "Progress slowly to avoid finger overload, especially on hard boulders." }
      ]
    },
    {
