      "title": "Heel Hook",
      "lastEdited": "2026-03-14T09:25:00.000Z",
      "content": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "text": "A heel hook uses the heel on a hold to create pulling tension and body control." },
        { "type": "list", "style": "bulleted", "items": ["Great for keeping tension", "Useful on steep terrain", "Common in intermediate sequences"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gaston",
      "title": "Gaston",
      "lastEdited": "2026-03-14T09:30:00.000Z",
      "content": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "text": "A gaston is a side-pull position where the elbow points outward while pushing away." },
        { "type": "list", "style": "bulleted", "items": ["Requires shoulder stability", "Common in vertical to overhung climbing", "Appears often in technical routes"] }
      ]
    },
    {
